**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The code seeds are exported once into the shipped catalogue (001 §B 'Shipped catalogue': GUIDs and values byte-for-byte; .spec-md §3.5, §3.6, §7 'Code seeds → catalogue files'). (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx`, the throw-away tool. It `#I`s `../OpticalConstructor.Tests/bin/x64/Release/net10.0/`, the Release x64 output that holds the built Domain and Storage assemblies beside every assembly they load. From there it `#r`s `Softellect.Berreman.OpticalConstructor.Domain.dll`, `Softellect.Berreman.OpticalConstructor.Storage.dll` and the assemblies they load, each from that folder (among them Softellect.Sys, the Berreman core, MathNet.Numerics, FSharp.SystemTextJson, and JsonSchema.Net with Json.More and JsonPointer.Net). It uses no `#r "nuget:"`, so no network is needed. It seals every seed step 34 names at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, through step 25's builders and step 30's `sealed`. It builds `CatalogueData.tryCreate CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (CatalogueName "Built-in") VersionNumber.first` and writes it with `(CatalogueProxy.create (FolderName (Path.Combine(__SOURCE_DIRECTORY__, "Builtin")))).writeCatalogue` (step 33). So the committed files are exactly what the product writer writes, and no second writer exists. Any `Error` prints its case and exits with 1. (2) Build the solution, run `dotnet fsi Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx` once from the repository root, and commit `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/`. It holds `.catalogue-json` and one file per seed, named by the entry's name made safe (step 24's `FileStem`) plus its kind's extension, with no category folders (001 §A): `Silicon.material-json`, `Nd_YAG ×2 532 nm.source-json` and the rest, exactly the files this step's effects list. Every file is LF-only and ends with one LF (step 30). `git check-ignore` MUST report none of them: `[Bb]in/` (`.gitignore:23`) does not match `Builtin/`, and only `*.tmp` (`.gitignore:78`) would match, which is intended, since no `.tmp` is committed. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` gains, beside its `schema` `Content` items, `<Content Include="..\Catalogue\Builtin\**" Link="Catalogue\Builtin\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)">` with `<CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>`, and no new comment. So every output that references Storage carries the same files, as it carries `schema/` today: the App (`<install>\Catalogue\Builtin\`), the TestWindows heads and both constructor test suites. No product code reads them yet (S1.6 does), and the seeds stay until S1.7.

**Acceptance.** After the catalogue is exported and copied, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the built-in catalogue is the Built-in catalogue at version 1`, `every built-in material and category in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in sample in the catalogue equals its seed`, `every built-in source, detector and polarizer in the catalogue equals its seed` and `the built-in catalogue is exactly what the seeds seal to, and its manifest hash is stable`, which step 34 left red; `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/` MUST hold exactly `.catalogue-json` and the entry files this step's effects list, none of them git-ignored; and build, elevation and the six s05 invariants MUST pass.
